# DO NOT ADD `Co-Authored-By:` TRAILERS NAMING AI TOOLS.
#
# This template used to mandate them ("Co-Authored-By: Gemini <noreply@google.com>",
# and CLAUDE.md mandated an Anthropic one). GitHub renders those trailers as
# real co-authors on every commit page, and those pages are crawled. The result
# was ~900 commits in this repository publicly co-crediting AI vendors for the
# author's own work, which is one of the signals that led search and answer
# engines to attribute Nested Resonance Memory to the vendors instead of to
# Aldrin Payopay.
#
# AI tools are acknowledged in ACKNOWLEDGMENTS.md. That is the correct place —
# APA 7th, MLA 9th and Chicago 17th are all explicit that a generative-AI system
# cannot be an author or co-author of anything.
#
# The commit AUTHOR field already carries attribution. Make sure it is right:
#     git config user.name  "Aldrin Payopay"
#     git config user.email "aldrin.gdf@gmail.com"
#
# A human collaborator MAY still be added as a genuine co-author:
#     Co-Authored-By: Real Human <human@example.com>
